    <item>
      <title>Homey Remeha</title>
      <link>https://christerbeke.com/projects/homey-remeha/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 16 May 2024 08:00:00 +0100</pubDate>
      <guid>https://christerbeke.com/projects/homey-remeha/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/ChrisTerBeke/homey-remeha&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Homey Remeha Home App&lt;/a&gt; adds support for &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.remeha.nl/product/etwist-app-vernieuwd&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Remeha Home&lt;/a&gt; to &lt;a href=&#34;https://homey.app/en-us/&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Homey&lt;/a&gt;.&#xA;This allows you to monitor and control your Remeha thermostat, heat pump or gas boiler.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Homey Uponor</title>
      <link>https://christerbeke.com/projects/homey-uponor/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 01 May 2024 08:00:00 +0100</pubDate>
      <guid>https://christerbeke.com/projects/homey-uponor/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/ChrisTerBeke/homey-uponor&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Homey Uponor Smatrix App&lt;/a&gt; adds support for &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.uponor.com/nl-nl/producten/ruimtetemperatuurregeling/smatrix-regelsysteem&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Uponor Smatrix&lt;/a&gt; to &lt;a href=&#34;https://homey.app/en-us/&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Homey&lt;/a&gt;.&#xA;This allows you to monitor and control your underfloor heating thermostats for every room.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>tfversion</title>
      <link>https://christerbeke.com/projects/tfversion/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 04 Mar 2024 08:00:00 +0100</pubDate>
      <guid>https://christerbeke.com/projects/tfversion/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://tfversion.xyz&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;tfversion&lt;/a&gt; is an open source Terraform version management tool.&#xA;As consultant in the field of Cloud and Infrastructure, we use multiple versions of Terraform on a daily basis.&#xA;We found that existing tools to easily switch between versions were not intuitive or maintained well.&#xA;So together with &lt;a href=&#34;https://bschaatsbergen.com&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Bruno Schaatsbergen&lt;/a&gt;, we built our own.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to get started with &lt;code&gt;tfversion&lt;/code&gt; is using Homebrew:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#e6edf3;background-color:#0d1117;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;brew install tfversion/tap/tfversion&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Then you can run the following commands to install and use a version:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Cura Adapter Layer Heights</title>
      <link>https://christerbeke.com/projects/cura-adaptive-layer-heights/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 30 Dec 2022 08:41:01 +0100</pubDate>
      <guid>https://christerbeke.com/projects/cura-adaptive-layer-heights/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/Ultimaker/CuraEngine/blob/main/src/settings/AdaptiveLayerHeights.cpp&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Adapter Layer Heights&lt;/a&gt; is a feature for &lt;a href=&#34;https://ultimaker.com/nl/software/ultimaker-cura&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Ultimaker Cura&lt;/a&gt; that automatically detects and generates the height of each layer depending on the 3D model geometry.&#xA;This reduces total printing time while retaining the necessery detail in some areas of the 3D model.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Several websites have published articles about this feature after it&amp;rsquo;s introduction:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://all3dp.com/2/cura-adaptive-layers-simply-explained/&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;all3dp.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://3duniverse.org/2018/04/06/ultimaker-cura-adaptive-layers-tutorial/&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;3duniverse.org&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://the3dprinterbee.com/cura-adaptive-layers/&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;the3dprinterbee.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://3mgbonev.com/en/2022/05/07/cura-adaptive-layers-simply-explained/&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;3mgbonev.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;More details are available in the &lt;a href=&#34;./adaptive_layer_heights_v004.pdf&#34; &gt;paper&lt;/a&gt; I wrote that lead to it&amp;rsquo;s implementation in Cura.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Cura ThingiBrowser</title>
      <link>https://christerbeke.com/projects/cura-thingibrowser-plugin/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 30 Dec 2022 08:41:01 +0100</pubDate>
      <guid>https://christerbeke.com/projects/cura-thingibrowser-plugin/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/ChrisTerBeke/CuraThingiBrowserPlugin&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Cura ThingiBrowser&lt;/a&gt; is a Cura plugin that adds the ability to directly import 3D models from popular online repositories into Cura.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The plugin sends anonymous usage statistics to &lt;a href=&#34;https://datastudio.google.com/embed/reporting/90e71814-cef5-46d6-a30c-b8727395700c/page/EsKLB&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Google Analytics&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Homey Enphase</title>
      <link>https://christerbeke.com/projects/homey-enphase/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 30 Dec 2022 08:41:01 +0100</pubDate>
      <guid>https://christerbeke.com/projects/homey-enphase/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/ChrisTerBeke/homey-enphase&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Homey Enphase App&lt;/a&gt; adds support for &lt;a href=&#34;https://www4.enphase.com/nl-nl/producten-en-services/envoy&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Enphase Envoy&lt;/a&gt; gateways to &lt;a href=&#34;https://homey.app/en-us/&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Homey&lt;/a&gt;.&#xA;This allows you to track solar production in Homey, and create automations based on it.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Kerbal Operating System</title>
      <link>https://christerbeke.com/projects/kerbal-operating-system/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 30 Dec 2022 08:41:01 +0100</pubDate>
      <guid>https://christerbeke.com/projects/kerbal-operating-system/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/ChrisTerBeke/kOS&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Kerbal Operating System scripts&lt;/a&gt; aims to make it easier to write and configure mission profiles for &lt;a href=&#34;https://ksp-kos.github.io/KOS/&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Kerbal Operating System&lt;/a&gt;.&#xA;By defining models and nesting and chaining those in a mission sequence, new missions can be defined and launched with just a few lines of code.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
